==Lore==
<tabber>
 Beginnings=
The Perseus was first constructed in the late 2520s, a few years before the [[Xi'an-Human Cold War]]. These gunships were frequently deployed along the [[Perry Line]], making them a regular fixture after Xi'an-Human first Contact in 2530.<ref name="PerseusBrochure">{{Cite RSI|url=https://media.robertsspaceindustries.com/7z87yphjoj2jk/source.pdf|text=Perseus - brochure|accessdate=2020-11-28}}</ref>
|-|
 Retired=
In 2863, RSI retired the Perseus from production due to a lack of interest from the UEEN.<ref name="PerseusBrochure"/>
|-|
 Vanduul War=
During [[Operation Mandrake]] in [[2946]] in the [[Vanduul War]], the aging Perseus ''[[UEES Achilles]]'' managed to take down two Vanduul destroyers when the ship was damaged beyond repair. Due to its performance, UEEN Admiral [[Ernst Bishop]] personally lobbied RSI to start producing Perseus models again for use against the [[Vanduul]].<ref name="PerseusBrochure"/>
|-|
 Civilian version=
Following Perseus success against the Vanduul, RSI expanded development to include a civilian version under the [[Militia Mobilization Initiative]].<ref name="galactapedia">{{Cite RSI|url=https://robertsspaceindustries.com/galactapedia/article/bEzXg6qGe6-perseus|text=Galactapedia: Perseus|accessdate=2023-04-20}}</ref> The new Perseus, equipped with modernized weapons and a redesigned lower deck that could accommodate cargo vehicles<ref name="PerseusBrochure"/> was released on day 9 of the [[Intergalactic Aerospace Expo 2950]] <ref name="iae2950yt">[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oPO7lm84LWc Star Citizen: IAE 2950 - Roberts Space Industries] on YouTube</ref> event.
</tabber>

