==Development==
{{Timeline styles}}
{| class="timeline"
|-
|2020-07
|John Crewe put together the design brief. Paul Jones and Gavin Rothery created the concept artwork, with principle work beginning in July 2020.
|-
|2020-11-28
|The Perseus was publicly revealed during [[Intergalactic Aerospace Expo 2950|IAE 2950]].
|-
|2020-12-18
|Chris Roberts wanted a ship that stood apart from the standard battleship or the destroyers, torpedo boats, carriers, etc already added to the line-up. He chose the ironclad gunboat as the inspiration. In the initial stages, the Perseus' was referred to as "RSI Gunboat", not receiving its final name until very late in the concept development process.<ref name="JP812">{{Cite RSI|url=https://robertsspaceindustries.com/media/wcsmbufcvqphvr/source/JP08-12-DEC-Its-A-Gas.pdf|text=Jump Point Issue 8-12 December 2020: "It's A Gas"|accessdate=2023-07-21}}</ref>
|-
|2025-11-19
|The Perseus became flyable with the launch of [[Update:Star Citizen Alpha 4.4.0|Alpha 4.4.0]], but is to be properly unveiled on RSI day of [[Intergalactic Aerospace Expo 2955|IAE 2955]].
|-
|}

==Trivia==
* In Greek mythology, Perseus, son of Danae and Zeus, is recognized as the fabled founder of the Perseid dynasty. Alongside figures such as Cadmus and Bellerophon, he stands as one of the most prominent Greek heroes and a renowned monster slayer prior to the era of Heracles. Perseus famously decapitated the Gorgon Medusa on behalf of Polydectes and rescued Andromeda from the clutches of the sea monster Cetus.<ref>Wikipedia Perseus https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perseus</ref>
* Perseus is also a constellation located in the northern hemisphere that is named after the legendary Greek hero. It features the luminous star [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpha_Persei Mirfak], the variable star [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algol Algol], and serves as the radiant point for the yearly [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perseids Perseid meteor shower] which is observable between the months of July and August.

